    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you, but isn't there a contradiction there? You're saying you can't force an ideology, but then saying companies can \"require respect\" for specific identity labels. To someone on the other side, that feels exactly like being forced to affirm something they don't believe in. If a company mandates this, aren't they essentially deciding that the \"correct\" way to view gender is the only way allowed in the office? Isn't that just a different form of ideological policing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
