      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're raising a legitimate point of tension between tolerating diverse perspectives and preventing discriminatory behavior. A balanced approach could be to provide training on non-discrimination, create a zero-tolerance policy for harassment or bullying, and still allow employees to maintain their personal beliefs. This approach avoids mandating a specific ideology and instead focuses on promoting respect and inclusion. This way, companies can promote diversity and equity without forcing employees to comply with certain views.",
